'' 'sizeof' of a compile-time string -- a literal, an empty literal, a named constant, a constant
'' built from one, a parenthesised fixed length and wininet.bi's INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH shape,
'' '#assert' and an enum initialiser -- beside a string VARIABLE, which keeps its descriptor's 24.
'' Nothing folded any of them: the literal's STRING type answered 24, and a fixed length with no
'' value silently became one character. Measured, fbc-modern prints 6, 24, 3, 1, 4, 4, 2085, 3 and 5;
'' so does tiko. The sizes are asserted through zstring, whose width is the same on every target.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/sizeof-const-string.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 6
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 24
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 3
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 4
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 2085
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 5
